[{"body":"Can you add newly created benchmark data to zenodo, so we not loose it, document it, what do you need for this ?","comments":[],"number":8,"title":"Add benchmark data to zenodo","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T20:50:05Z"},{"body":"Make a strategy for optimization like if a commit of the tool perforce well continue from there but if it does not further improvement pick other commit and combine ideas make like a flowchart and add to docs and readme","comments":[],"number":7,"title":"Optimization plan","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T20:48:42Z"},{"body":"Try to optimize tool and parameters to use less time and resources but aim for similar or better performane, think about good performane measured numbet of bins, contigs size, compl. Cont. F1 score check cami papers for infos \nMaybe perams can be automatically set based on input file size or contig stats","comments":[],"number":6,"title":"Optimization","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T20:46:38Z"},{"body":"Use bioinformatic tools to make a small test benchmark dataset (maybe based on one of the dataset already used), and potentially fix issues with the tool if it does not work with the small dataset. Make the dataset as small as possible. But the tool should still use its real logic. Parameters can be changed, though.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWbLpVg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"U should for all functional tests use the small test data, log it as always, then make a medium size benchmakr dataset once the tests work and and only after major commits run on big benchmark data","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:41:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5799864662","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWbNYYw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Also make a plan which benchmark data to use human as host should be included so you do not excede the space limit on the drive","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:43:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5799893091","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWcQ2Xg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Small dataset ready + both new directives addressed\n\n**Small dataset (built):** `/vol/data/datasets/comebin_small` (94 MB) — top-300 contigs by length from the demo BATS metagenome (marker-gene carrying) + all reads overlapping them via `bedtools intersect -abam … -b contigs.bed -u` (params changeable). Test runner `scripts/run_small_test.sh` writes full run bookkeeping (run_meta + command lines, comebin_run.log, resources sampler). The test-run itself is queued behind the in-progress baseline run (CPU policy: no concurrent timed runs) — results will be posted here right after.\n\n**Directive 1 — functional tests always on small data, benchmarks only after major commits:** recorded in `docs/07-fix-batches.md` + `docs/08` and adopted as the workflow: every fix batch / new version is validated on `comebin_small` (minutes, logged as usual); full timed benchmark + CheckM2/CheckM eval only for major commits.\n\n**Directive 2 — dataset & disk-space plan incl. human host-associated data:** `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`. Summary: 492 GB volume, **391 GB free** now; planned additions ≈ demo 6.4 + small 0.1 + CAMI II marine (1–2 samples, 10–20 GB) + **human host-associated CAMI II** (Multisample Human Microbiome Project DOI 10.4126/frl01-006425518, or Toy Human Microbiome — 49 samples across 5 body sites; plan 1–2 samples ≤ 30 GB) + CAMI III (≤ 50 GB, sizes verified before download) ≈ **≤ 100 GB total → fits with >50 GB headroom**. Cleanup policy: delete source archives after md5/gzip-verified extraction, keep provenance (md5 + listings) in docs.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5800998494","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWclGfQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Supervisor follow-up: explicit medium stage + safe test runner\n\nAcknowledged the **18:51 UTC edit**. The workflow is now explicitly:\n\n1. run/log the real-pipeline functional test on the 94 MB small set;\n2. after that passes, build/run a medium derived benchmark (initial target 3,000 contigs, hard cap 5 GB, with measured provenance/size);\n3. reserve the large benchmark for post-major-commit runs.\n\nThis is now recorded in `docs/06-benchmark-commands.md`, `docs/07-fix-batches.md`, and `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`.\n\nSupervisor commit `899f7e7` also closes runner gaps found during verification: `run_small_test.sh` now refuses overlap/overwrite, supports either the pristine or v1.1.0 source, passes safe CPU/seed/small-batch parameters, records the promised 30-second resource timeline, and hands off atomically to the benchmark watchdog. `run_eval.sh` refuses to overlap the registered benchmark.\n\nNo small end-to-end result is being claimed yet, and the medium set has intentionally **not** been built while the active baseline is running. Those remain gated on the small COMEBin + CheckM2/CheckM run.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T19:19:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/2#issuecomment-5801330301","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":2,"title":"Can you try to create a small benchmark dataset for comebin ?","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T19:19:23Z"},{"body":"## How this works\n\nThis issue (and any issue you open in this repo) is read by the benchmark agent on a\nrolling basis — it replies here with status/answers, and its restart prompt tells it to\ncheck issues first.\n\n**How to give an idea:** open a new issue (or comment here) with as much detail as you\nhave. Examples of what the agent can act on:\n\n- \"try binners X and Y on the CAMI II dataset\" — gets executed and recorded in `docs/` + `results/`\n- \"COMEBin/src/cluster.py line N is wrong, do Y\" — becomes a fix batch on branch `comebin-optimizations`\n- \"change threads / add parameter sweeps\" — benchmark config change\n\n**Conventions the agent follows:**\n\n- every answer/implementation is documented in `docs/03-fixes.md` (fix batches) or\n  `docs/01-datasets.md` (datasets) and referenced from the issue\n- benchmark results land in `results/` as one CSV per run\n- current task state: `PROGRESS.md`\n\n---\n*agent note: this issue was created by the agent as a starting point; see\n`docs/05-agent-restart.md` for how the agent is woken/resumed.*","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWYioNQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Status update (agent, 2026-09-23 ~14:55Z):\n- Baseline COMEBin demo run in progress (training phase, ~30 cores, unmodified commit 987db95) -> CheckM2/CheckM + README table next.\n- Repos/docs/scripts live; watch our status via README line 1 or status/status.log.\n- Responding to issue #2 (small benchmark dataset) right now.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T14:53:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/1#issuecomment-5797095477","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1,"title":"Idea inbox: benchmark ideas, COMEBin fixes, dataset requests","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T14:53:13Z"}]

