[0m$ [0mnl -ba docs/09-optimization-strategy.md | sed -n '1,55p'
1	# Optimization strategy (issue #7)
     2	
     3	Goal: **reduce COMEBin runtime and resource use while keeping quality the same or
     4	better**, judged with the exact same benchmark harness as the baseline so every
     5	decision is data-driven.
     6	
     7	## What we measure (fixed, per run)
     8	
     9	| Metric | Source | Why |
    10	|---|---|---|
    11	| Wall-clock time (total + per stage) | `runs/<run>/run_meta.txt` + run log | primary speed target |
    12	| Peak RAM | `logs/resources.tsv` (30-s samples) | primary resource target |
    13	| CPU time / core-hours | run log + resources.tsv | efficiency |
    14	| # bins (≥200 kb filter noted) | CheckM run output | productivity measure |
    15	| CheckM2 mean completeness / contamination | `run_eval.sh` | quality (main) |
    16	| CheckM v1 mean completeness / contamination | `run_eval.sh` | quality (cross-check) |
    17	| CAMI-style F1 (harmonic mean of completeness and purity) | CAMI II/III GT once available | CAMI benchmark metric, see CAMI papers |
    18	
    19	"Good performance" is therefore: **more headroom on # bins / completeness /
    20	contamination / F1 per unit of time×RAM**. See `docs/04-evaluation.md` for
    21	metric definitions and the CAMI papers in the README references.
    22	
    23	## Process: batched commits with a decision gate
    24	
    25	Optimization work happens on a branch (`comebin-optimizations-v11`), **one commit
    26	per batch** (see `docs/07-fix-batches.md`). Each batch goes through the gate below.
    27	
    28	```mermaid
    29	flowchart TD
    30	    A[Pick candidate change / param from idea list] --> B[Small functional test<br/>small dataset, fast]
    31	    B -->|FAIL| G[Investigate, fix, or drop the idea]
    32	    G --> A
    33	    B -->|PASS| C[Benchmark on small/medium set]
    34	    C --> D{Better or equal<br/>time AND quality?}
    35	    D -->|YES| E[KEEP commit, record results in results/ and commit msg]
    36	    E --> F[Continue: next batch from this commit]
    37	    D -->|NO| H[Revert or rework this commit]
    38	    H --> I[Combine with other surviving ideas<br/>and re-test as a new batch]
    39	    I --> A
    40	    F --> J[After major commits: full large benchmark<br/>e.g. COMEBin demo / CAMI II marine / CAMI III]
    41	```
    42	
    43	Invariants:
    44	
    45	- **Never skip the small functional test.** Any change that breaks the small run
    46	  is not benchmarked further.
    47	- **Baseline first:** every optimization is compared against the unmodified
    48	  baseline run (`runs/baseline_unmodified`) and, where applicable, the previous
    49	  kept commit.
    50	- **One timed thing at a time:** no concurrent COMEBin/CheckM runs, so timings
    51	  stay comparable.
    52	- **Record or reject:** a commit is kept *only* if the evidence says keep;
    53	  otherwise it is reverted or reworked and combined with other ideas.
    54	- Cost guardrail: if we accrue several sequential failures, go back and pick a
    55	  different idea (per the flowchart) instead of spending more time on a dead end.
